  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "criterion": "`registerWorkspaceRoutes()` accepts an `ErrorLogManager` parameter (6th argument), and `index.ts` passes it.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`POST /api/projects/:id/workspaces/:wid/launch/vscode` returns 404 when the workspace does not exist.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`POST /api/projects/:id/workspaces/:wid/launch/vscode` returns 400 with `\"Workspace file does not exist. Run setup first.\"` when the `.code-workspace` file is missing from disk.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`POST /api/projects/:id/workspaces/:wid/launch/vscode` returns `200 { success: true }` when the file exists and the launch succeeds.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`POST /api/projects/:id/workspaces/:wid/launch/github-desktop/:rid` returns 404 when the workspace or project/repository is not found.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`POST /api/projects/:id/workspaces/:wid/launch/github-desktop/:rid` returns 400 with `\"Repository directory does not exist. Run setup first.\"` when the repo directory is missing.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`POST /api/projects/:id/workspaces/:wid/launch/github-desktop/:rid` returns `200 { success: true }` when the directory exists and the launch succeeds.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "On launch failure, both endpoints return 500 with a descriptive error message and log an entry to the error log with `Source: 'app-launcher'` and appropriate `Operation`, `Severity: 'error'`, `Context`, and `Message` fields.",
      "met": true
    }
  ],
  "active_pipeline_stages": [
    "implementation",
    "qa",
    "security-audit",
    "code-review",
    "documentation"
  ],
  "revision": 0,
  "pipelines": [
    {
      "type": "implementation",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-04-15T09:48:38Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-04-15T09:58:01Z",
      "duration_ms": 563000,
      "summary": [
        "Added `ErrorLogManager` as 6th parameter to `registerWorkspaceRoutes()` in workspaces.ts, plus an optional 7th `launchFn` parameter (defaults to real `launchApplication`) for test injection.",
        "Imported `ErrorLogManager` (type-only) and `launchApplication` in workspaces.ts.",
        "Added `POST /api/projects/:id/workspaces/:wid/launch/vscode` handler: verifies workspace exists (404), checks .code-workspace file on disk (400 with exact message), launches via `launchFn('code', [filePath])`, returns 200 {success:true} on success, 500 + error log on failure.",
        "Added `POST /api/projects/:id/workspaces/:wid/launch/github-desktop/:rid` handler: verifies workspace (404), verifies project + repo membership via ProjectManager (404), checks repo dir on disk (400 with exact message), launches via `launchFn('github', [repoDir])`, returns 200 {success:true} on success, 500 + error log on failure.",
        "Both 500 paths log to ErrorLogManager with Source: 'app-launcher', correct Operation, Severity: 'error', Context with ProjectId/WorkspaceId (and RepositoryId for github-desktop).",
        "Updated `index.ts` to pass `errorLogManager` as 6th arg to `registerWorkspaceRoutes()`.",
        "Updated existing `workspaces.test.ts` and `workspaces-health.test.ts` to pass stub 6th arg — no test regressions.",
        "Created `workspaces-launch.test.ts` with 14 new tests covering all 8 acceptance criteria scenarios. All 733 tests pass."
      ],
      "artifacts": {
        "files_modified": [
          "src/server/routes/workspaces.ts",
          "src/server/index.ts",
          "src/server/__tests__/routes/workspaces.test.ts",
          "src/server/__tests__/routes/workspaces-health.test.ts",
          "src/server/__tests__/routes/workspaces-launch.test.ts"
        ]
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-15T09:58:01Z",
          "note": "The optional 7th `launchFn` parameter on `registerWorkspaceRoutes()` is documented as 'for testing only'. A cleaner alternative would be a separate `LaunchService` interface injected at construction time, but the current approach is pragmatic and consistent with the existing codebase's style of passing flat dependencies."
        },
        {
          "type": "convention",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-15T09:58:01Z",
          "note": "workspaces.ts now has two different 404 patterns for the github-desktop route: WorkspaceManager throws NotFoundError for an unknown project (caught and forwarded), while ProjectManager.getById returns null (checked with an explicit if). This asymmetry is pre-existing in the codebase (see regenerate-workspace-file handler) but is worth noting for future consistency work."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-15T09:58:01Z",
          "note": "src/server/routes/workspaces.ts: The workspace-existence check at the top of both new handlers is copy-pasted from existing handlers (setup, health, regenerate-workspace-file). A small private helper `verifyWorkspaceExists(res, projectId, workspaceId): boolean` would reduce this duplication across 5+ handlers."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "qa",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-04-15T09:58:15Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-04-15T10:00:29Z",
      "duration_ms": 134000,
      "summary": [
        "Build check passed: `npm run build` (tsc) produced zero errors.",
        "All 733 tests passed (0 failures, 0 skipped). This includes 14 new tests in workspaces-launch.test.ts that directly cover all 8 acceptance criteria.",
        "All 8 AC explicitly verified against the implementation in workspaces.ts and corresponding test assertions.",
        "Regression confirmed: all pre-existing 719 tests continue to pass — workspaces.test.ts and workspaces-health.test.ts were correctly updated to pass the new 6th arg stub.",
        "Edge-case analysis completed: path traversal via repoId is blocked by `project.Repositories.includes(repoId)` combined with kebab-case ID validation at repo creation time; non-Error thrown objects are handled with fallback message in both 500 paths; concurrent launch requests are safe and by design; existsSync-on-directory edge case is benign given the use case."
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "test_coverage": "All 8 AC covered by 14 dedicated tests in workspaces-launch.test.ts",
        "tests_passed": 733,
        "tests_failed": 0
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:00:29Z",
          "note": "workspaces.ts launch/vscode handler: `fs.existsSync(wsFilePath)` returns true for directories as well as files. If a directory was created at the workspace file path, the 400 guard would be bypassed and `launchFn('code', [dirPath])` would be called. This is benign (VS Code opens directories) but worth noting for completeness — consistent with other handlers in the codebase."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:00:29Z",
          "note": "workspaces.ts launch/github-desktop handler: repoId path-traversal is effectively blocked by the `project.Repositories.includes(repoId)` check combined with kebab-case validation at repository creation time. No additional sanitization is needed, but a brief inline comment would aid future maintainers."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:00:29Z",
          "note": "Both new handlers share a copy-pasted workspace-existence check with 5+ other handlers (setup, health, regenerate-workspace-file, etc.). This pre-existing pattern was flagged by the Developer as a refactor opportunity. Not a defect — no action required for this WP."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "security-audit",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-04-15T10:00:53Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-04-15T10:02:23Z",
      "duration_ms": 90000,
      "summary": [
        "Reviewed 5 files (workspaces.ts, index.ts, app-launcher.ts, error-log.manager.ts, router.ts). All OWASP Top 10 categories evaluated. 0 Critical, 0 High findings. 2 Medium observations recorded (path traversal defence could be hardened with explicit normalisation; error message disclosure in 500 paths). Security sign-off: PASS."
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "security_issues": 0
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "risk",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:02:23Z",
          "note": "A03/A01 — Path Traversal (defence-in-depth gap): workspaces.ts lines 403 and 462. Both new handlers construct filesystem paths by joining `appConfig.projectsFolder`, `projectId`, `workspaceId`, and (for github-desktop) `repoId` via `path.join()`. These values originate from URL parameters extracted by the router. The router's `extractParams()` captures raw URL path segments without percent-decoding or normalisation — a segment value of `..` would survive extraction. For the github-desktop handler, `project.Repositories.includes(repoId)` provides the primary guard (the repository must be in the project's allow-list), so traversal via `repoId` is effectively blocked as long as ID values are validated at creation time (confirmed by QA). For `projectId` and `workspaceId`, there is no explicit traversal check in these two new handlers; traversal is only blocked indirectly by `workspaceManager.getById()` / `projectManager.getById()` lookup failures — callers can only reach a path if the manager returns a valid record for those IDs. This layered defence is adequate for the current localhost-only threat model, but adding explicit `path.resolve()` + `startsWith(appConfig.projectsFolder)` assertions would remove all doubt and future-proof the code if the server ever moves to a networked deployment. Remediation: add a guard such as `if (!resolvedPath.startsWith(path.resolve(appConfig.projectsFolder))) { sendError(res, 400, 'Invalid path.'); return; }` after constructing `wsFilePath` (line 403) and `repoDir` (line 462)."
        },
        {
          "type": "risk",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:02:23Z",
          "note": "A05 — Error Message Information Disclosure: workspaces.ts lines 413 and 472. On launch failure, the raw `err.message` from `launchApplication` is forwarded directly to the HTTP response body (500) AND to the error log. The launcher error messages include the executable name (e.g. `Failed to launch application \"code\": spawn code ENOENT`). In a multi-user or network-accessible environment this would disclose internal path structure. In the current threat model (localhost single-user CLI tool, server binds to 127.0.0.1 per index.ts:176) this is low practical risk, but is worth noting. Remediation: consider mapping internal error messages to a generic user-facing message (e.g. `'Failed to launch VS Code. Ensure VS Code is installed and available on PATH.'`) while preserving the full message only in the error log entry."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:02:23Z",
          "note": "A09 — Security Logging Coverage: Both new handlers log errors to ErrorLogManager on 500, with well-structured fields (Source, Operation, Severity, Context including ProjectId/WorkspaceId/RepositoryId). No gaps identified. Logging is absent for 400/404 responses, consistent with the existing codebase pattern — these are client errors and do not represent security events in this context."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:02:23Z",
          "note": "A07 — Authentication/Authorization: These endpoints perform no authentication or session checks — consistent with the rest of the codebase. The server binds exclusively to 127.0.0.1 (index.ts line 176), restricting access to the local machine. No auth gap introduced by the new endpoints."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:02:23Z",
          "note": "A06 — Dependencies: No new third-party dependencies were introduced. The implementation uses only Node.js built-ins (`node:child_process`, `node:fs`, `node:path`) and existing internal modules. No CVE exposure added."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:02:23Z",
          "note": "A08 — Software & Data Integrity / Command Injection: app-launcher.ts uses `spawn()` with `shell: false` on non-Windows platforms, which prevents shell injection via the args array. On Windows, `shell: true` is used for `.cmd` launcher compatibility — the `command` argument is a hardcoded string literal ('code' or 'github') supplied by the route handler, not user-controlled input, so shell injection is not a risk in practice."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:02:23Z",
          "note": "Full OWASP Top 10 review summary: A01 (Access Control) — workspace/project membership validated before filesystem access; A02 (Crypto) — no cryptographic operations introduced; A03 (Injection) — spawn args are derived from validated IDs + config paths, not raw user input; A04 (Insecure Design) — guard ordering is correct (entity existence before disk check before launch); A05 (Misconfiguration) — stack traces not leaked, generic 500 messages used except for launcher errors (noted above); A06 (Components) — no new deps; A07 (Auth) — localhost-only server, no regression; A08 (Integrity) — no unsafe deserialization or unsigned updates; A09 (Logging) — error log entries correctly structured; A10 (SSRF) — no outbound HTTP requests; no server-side URL fetching introduced."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "status_changed_at": "2026-04-15T09:48:38Z",
  "last_updated": "2026-04-15T10:02:23Z",
  "handoff_notes": [
    {
      "from_agent": "Developer",
      "to_agent": "QA",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-15T09:58:01Z",
      "notes": [
        "\"All 8 acceptance criteria are met and verified by 14 dedicated tests in workspaces-launch.test.ts. The injectable `launchFn` parameter (7th arg, optional, defaults to real `launchApplication`) is the test seam — QA tests should use this same mechanism. The route for github-desktop does a double 404 check: first via WorkspaceManager (throws NotFoundError for unknown project), then via ProjectManager.getById (null for unknown project) + Repositories.includes (for unknown repo). The workspace file path for vscode uses the same `getWorkspaceFilePath()` helper used by the regenerate-workspace-file route.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "QA",
      "to_agent": "Security Auditor",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:00:29Z",
      "notes": [
        "All 8 acceptance criteria verified and met. 733/733 tests pass. Build is clean. Two new POST routes (launch/vscode, launch/github-desktop/:rid) are correctly implemented with proper 404/400/200/500 handling and ErrorLogManager integration. No security concerns beyond what is noted in comments (existsSync-on-directory is benign; repoId traversal is blocked by existing validation). Ready for Security Audit."
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "Security Auditor",
      "to_agent": "Reviewer",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:02:23Z",
      "notes": [
        "Security audit PASS. No Critical or High findings. Two Medium observations raised (defence-in-depth path traversal hardening; error message disclosure in 500 paths) — neither blocks approval in the current localhost-only deployment context. All 8 acceptance criteria confirmed met. Ready for Code Review."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

